# .cursorrules - RetireFire Project Rules

---

## 🚫 NEVER BYPASS CHECKLIST (READ FIRST, EVERY TIME)

> [!CAUTION]
> **These rules are MANDATORY. Failure to follow them has caused bugs, broken builds, and wasted user time.**

### BEFORE ANY Code Change:
- [ ] ✅ Check `TASKS.md` - Is this work already done?
- [ ] ✅ Check `ISSUES.md` - Is this bug already tracked/fixed?
- [ ] ✅ Run `npm test` - Baseline must pass (231+ tests)
- [ ] ✅ Run `npm run build` - Build must succeed

### AFTER ANY Code Change:
- [ ] ✅ Run `npm test` again - No regressions allowed
- [ ] ✅ Run `npm run build` - Build must still work
- [ ] ✅ Update `ISSUES.md` if fixing a bug
- [ ] ✅ Update `TASKS.md` if completing a task
- [ ] ✅ Commit with descriptive message

### BEFORE Saying "DONE" or "FIXED":
- [ ] ✅ Provide EVIDENCE (test output, build log, or screenshot)
- [ ] ✅ Update ALL relevant documentation
- [ ] ✅ Verify the fix actually works (never assume)

### Documentation Must Be Updated:
| When you... | Update these files |
|------------|-------------------|
| Fix a bug | `ISSUES.md` (mark fixed), `TASKS.md` |
| Complete a task | `TASKS.md` (mark done) |
| Add a feature | `TASKS.md`, `README.md` if user-facing |
| Find a new issue | `ISSUES.md` (add with priority) |

**NEVER claim "fixed" or "complete" without updating documentation.**

---

## 🚨 CRITICAL SAFETY RULES

### NEVER RUN These Commands

**ABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN** - These commands can destroy the system:

### 🚨 MANDATORY: WSL Usage
- **ALWAYS use `wsl -d Ubuntu-22.04 <command>` for git and file system operations.**
- **Do NOT run raw Windows/PowerShell commands where WSL alternatives exist.**
- **Reason**: We are developing in a Windows environment but deploying/testing with Linux-based tools and standards.

```bash
rm -rf /
rm -rf ~
rm -rf *
format c:
del /f /s /q
rmdir /s /q
:(){:|:&};:
dd if=
mkfs.
> /dev/sda
chmod -R 777 /
```

**If any command looks suspicious or destructive, STOP and ask the user first.**

