## Code Quality Rules

### Testing
- ✅ All new features MUST include tests
- ✅ Maintain 100% test pass rate
- ✅ Run `npm test` before committing
- ✅ Run full suite before deployment

### Documentation
- ✅ Update TASKS.md when completing tasks
- ✅ Update ISSUES.md when fixing bugs
- ✅ Update PROJECT_STATUS.md for major changes
- ✅ Keep documentation current and consolidated

### Code Style
- ✅ Follow patterns in `/docs/guides/Coding_Standards.md`
- ✅ Use consistent naming conventions
- ✅ Comment complex logic
- ✅ Keep functions focused and small

---

## Project-Specific Rules

### Financial Calculations
- ✅ Always use `formatCurrency()` for money displays
- ✅ Always use `formatPercent()` for percentages
- ✅ Test all tax calculations
- ✅ Validate all projections

### Charts
- ✅ **EVERY CHART MUST HAVE WORKING TOOLTIPS ON HOVER** (CRITICAL)
- ✅ Verify tooltips manually or via test before marking "Done"
- ✅ Use consistent color palette
- ✅ Enable tooltips on all charts
- ✅ Update charts after data changes
- ✅ Test chart rendering

### Settings
- ✅ Save to localStorage after changes
- ✅ Validate input ranges
- ✅ Provide clear labels
- ✅ Show impact of changes
 
### Lessons Learned (Persistence Rules)
- ✅ **Import Verification**: When modularizing or adding logic, always verify that the main entry point (`main.js`) imports all necessary modules (e.g., `SimulationEngine`). Missing imports lead to silent browser failures even if unit tests pass.
- ✅ **Defensive Calculation**: Always use fallback patterns like `(config.settings?.personal?.retireAge || 65)` to prevent `NaN` or `undefined` issues when user configuration is incomplete or corrupted.
- ✅ **Chart State**: Always destroy existing chart instances using `destroyAllCharts()` or `destroyChart(id)` before recreating them to prevent Chart.js "Canvas is already in use" errors.
- ✅ **Logic Testing**: Maintain binary logic verification via `Diagnostic.test.js` to catch breaking changes in financial calculations without needing a full browser environment.
- ✅ **MCP Workspace Governance (Windows)**: For background agents on Windows, always prefer direct `node.exe` execution for MCP servers over `.cmd` wrappers to avoid path/permission issues. Ensure `--autoConnect` and appropriate `--remote-debugging-port` (default 9222) are used for Chrome tools.
- ✅ **Cache Management**: Always perform a `Ctrl + F5` (Hard Refresh) or clean `dist` build (`rm -rf dist` on bash or `Remove-Item -Recurse -Force dist` on PS) when UI changes do not appear on the live server, as Vite/DreamHost may serve stale assets.
- ✅ **Historical Market Patterns**: When implementing stress tests, use the sampling logic in `SimulationEngine.projectPath` with high-fidelity historical data (e.g., `src/data/HistoricalData.js`) to ensure statistical realism beyond standard standard deviation.
 
